            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Pat-Perry"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Oh my….was this ever good and so very easy! Summers in Maine are all about lobsters and corn! This time we decided to do the corn and potato salad after the messy lobsters. This allowed the corn to take center stage. It was so sweet and had a really nice crunch to it. It was freshly picked roadside corn, which is what we usually use. That being said it turned out better than any other time. I have always added the sugar but never the lemon juice. Definitely the best way ever.",
            "datePublished": "2026-07-25T11:50:46.017Z"
          },
          {
